{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8yMDIxL0tpbmclMjBPdHRvJTIwJTI4MjAyMSUyOS8","type":"movie","name":"King Otto","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/mOO8CQhljP8yCfwQgX9kbf8ez7p.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/sxM16ipmQE1oXKDrNu5CbyTSzow.jpg","description":"In the summer of 2004, audiences looked on in disbelief as the Greek National Football Team, a country that had never previously won a single match or even scored a goal in a major tournament, took down the giants of world football to become the unlikeliest of European Champions. The architect behind this unprecedented triumph was legendary German football coach ‘King’ Otto Rehhagel. After accomplishing every major success in Germany, he made the bold decision to leave all he knew behind and work in a foreign country with the underachieving Greek National Team. This is the story of how these two contrasting cultures came together to speak the same language and write a new chapter of Greek mythology.\n\nRated PG · Released 27 May 2021 · Greece, United Kingdom · Language: English · 80 min\nStudio: Cinema Nolita\n\nOn your server — Audio: English · Subtitle files: English","releaseInfo":"2021","genres":["Documentary","Hollywood"],"imdbRating":"7.4","runtime":"80 min","cast":["Otto Rehhagel","Traianos Dellas","Vassilis Gagatsis","Giorgos Karagounis","Antonios Nikopolidis","Giourkas Seitaridis","Ioannis Topalidis"],"director":["Christopher Andre Marks"],"released":"2021-05-27T00:00:00.000Z","slogan":"Ancient Greece had 12 gods, modern Greece has 11.","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Christopher Andre Marks","character":"Director"},{"name":"Otto Rehhagel","character":"Self","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/aw0XN1dSAv9EMz1A5GYIeSdqMxI.jpg"},{"name":"Traianos Dellas","character":"Self","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/llzOPvFaFsCElzpjtS46vpKL1Tc.jpg"},{"name":"Vassilis Gagatsis","character":"Self","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/yF